{
  "issue": "#4427",
  "description": "Surface & IA registry: every route family a bounded context contributes to a deployable, and the admin-web console/desk section it lives under, must be declared here before scripts/check-structure/ia-registry-guard.mjs will let the guard pass. A family is the top-level path segment of a contributed route (deployableContributions[].routes[].routePath in a context context.json, before any admin-web section prefix is applied). Once a family is registered, any context may attach a nested panel/tab/drawer under it (a route whose routePath starts with the same top-level segment) without a new entry — grafts stay cheap. A brand-new top-level segment for a deployable (or, for admin-web, a deployable+section pair) needs a new entry, which is a reviewed, deliberate act.",
  "guide": [
    "deployable: one of admin-web, marketplace-web, public-web.",
    "section: required for admin-web entries only, one of the WebHostSection values (access, catalog, commerce, growth, support, platform) from infrastructure/platform-runtime/web.ts; omit for marketplace-web/public-web.",
    "family: the top-level path segment (e.g. \"sessions\" for routePath \"sessions/:id\"); use an empty string only for a deployable root route (public-web welcome page).",
    "owningContext: the bounded context that established the family (informational provenance, validated only for existing as a real context name — not re-derived by the guard).",
    "purpose: a short, present-tense description of what the family is for."
  ],
